 [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-106594/selection/b99a41c2495bc5629f5e19e5dd0eb7719a9a673afa058fcedfb87312b0b99f96" :answer/id #uuid "91051d22-91ad-5de2-b85f-6a74a9362f7d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "t\\in (0,\\frac{\\pi }{2}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-106594/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "90aa46b7-1194-55ec-b241-acfe1d3d7d56" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-106594/selection/1be01a38655c9b80c5143f8e1af887b96d6afac0d8b99aa5a70070b461be0f30" :answer-field/choices ["q-106594/selection/1be01a38655c9b80c5143f8e1af887b96d6afac0d8b99aa5a70070b461be0f30" "q-106594/selection/11ea745910ff697b9055ddbb7e7b8a23d1d92eec0a8c07053d7df7aa989d1cf5" "q-106594/selection/b85ba2ba54d596653a563476b4f78775ae06d7693e7e2bfe7b1bde461b8c1155" "q-106594/selection/cf4007c3fa4151e57698e948ec1fea6bf9b3de5d146d298803d0412645d0248d" "q-106594/selection/b99a41c2495bc5629f5e19e5dd0eb7719a9a673afa058fcedfb87312b0b99f96"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-106594" :question/id #uuid "84a65d17-6fdc-5b99-a102-85790ba4c79f" :question/math-academy-id "q-106594" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14077122/assets/189bc3083101fa113811891be78d57b626acca68856318304266a1d16fc9e251.png)\n\nThe quarter-hyperbola above is defined by the parametric equations\n\n$$\nx=2\\operatorname{sec}⁡t,\\,y=\\sqrt{7}\\operatorname{tan}⁡t.\n$$\n\nWhat is the domain of the parameter $t?$" :question/worked-solution "The parametric equations of the full hyperbola are\n\n$$\nx=2\\operatorname{sec}⁡t,\\,y=\\sqrt{7}\\operatorname{tan}⁡t,\\,t\\in [-\\pi ,\\pi ],\\,t\\ne \\pm \\frac{\\pi }{2}.\n$$\n\nTo restrict the parameterization to a quarter-hyperbola, we refer to the diagram below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14077122/assets/5344a6c4972c03c9177419daa2f74be81ecabfad1db5c10f8dcbce794b07b265.png)\n\nWe can see that if we restrict $t$ to $(-\\frac{\\pi }{2},0],$ we get the quarter-hyperbola.\n\nTherefore, the parametric equations that describe the required quarter-hyperbola are\n\n$$\nx=2\\operatorname{sec}⁡t,\\,y=\\sqrt{7}\\operatorname{tan}⁡t,\\,t\\in (-\\frac{\\pi }{2},0].\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-106594/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "14527450-9b34-5982-9d87-b5a31870a70e"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-106594"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "q-89347"] :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14077122/assets/a2f0f570ecc68de1a5b34fb3bd1b341fc83a728b026b035dde848dbf986e441b.png)\n\nThe quarter-hyperbola above is defined by the parametric equations\n\n$$\nx=3\\operatorname{sec}⁡t,\\,y=\\sqrt{5}\\operatorname{tan}⁡t.\n$$\n\nWhat is the domain of the parameter $t?$" :question/worked-solution "The parametric equations of the full hyperbola are\n\n$$\nx=3\\operatorname{sec}⁡t,\\,y=\\sqrt{5}\\operatorname{tan}⁡t,\\,t\\in [-\\pi ,\\pi ],\\,t\\ne \\pm \\frac{\\pi }{2}.\n$$\n\nTo restrict the parameterization to a quarter-hyperbola, we refer to the diagram below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14077122/assets/e7ef7fd90c828767359daf69f68f406d61e3f82ad86b1f6b3a9480c99dedadf8.png)\n\nWe can see that if we restrict $t$ to $(-\\frac{\\pi }{2},0],$ we get the quarter-hyperbola.\n\nTherefore, the parametric equations that describe the required quarter-hyperbola are\n\n$$\nx=3\\operatorname{sec}⁡t,\\,y=\\sqrt{5}\\operatorname{tan}⁡t,\\,t\\in (-\\frac{\\pi }{2},0].\n$$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "q-106595/selection/b85ba2ba54d596653a563476b4f78775ae06d7693e7e2bfe7b1bde461b8c1155" :answer/id #uuid "62c4b341-d6fc-5436-a71a-9fb5f7c2bda2" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "t\\in [-\\pi ,-\\frac{\\pi }{2})\\cup (\\frac{\\pi }{2},\\pi ]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-106595/selection/11ea745910ff697b9055ddbb7e7b8a23d1d92eec0a8c07053d7df7aa989d1cf5" :answer/id #uuid "32611e94-a6ea-5996-a289-ad9daf18ed26" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "t\\in (-\\frac{\\pi }{2},\\frac{\\pi }{2})" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-106595/selection/1be01a38655c9b80c5143f8e1af887b96d6afac0d8b99aa5a70070b461be0f30" :answer/id #uuid "7f5bb85d-a604-5162-8187-c555ead05d9d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "t\\in (-\\frac{\\pi }{2},0]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-106595/selection/cf4007c3fa4151e57698e948ec1fea6bf9b3de5d146d298803d0412645d0248d" :answer/id #uuid "86a7c42d-a270-590f-a73b-723b78327120" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "t\\in [0,\\frac{\\pi }{2})" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-106595/selection/b99a41c2495bc5629f5e19e5dd0eb7719a9a673afa058fcedfb87312b0b99f96" :answer/id #uuid "877ec35a-e9ae-5673-b753-42788fb71b61" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "t\\in (0,\\frac{\\pi }{2}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-106595/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "3ae689d6-5ec3-53eb-abb6-a4b38fb1e20b" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-106595/selection/1be01a38655c9b80c5143f8e1af887b96d6afac0d8b99aa5a70070b461be0f30" :answer-field/choices ["q-106595/selection/b85ba2ba54d596653a563476b4f78775ae06d7693e7e2bfe7b1bde461b8c1155" "q-106595/selection/11ea745910ff697b9055ddbb7e7b8a23d1d92eec0a8c07053d7df7aa989d1cf5" "q-106595/selection/1be01a38655c9b80c5143f8e1af887b96d6afac0d8b99aa5a70070b461be0f30" "q-106595/selection/cf4007c3fa4151e57698e948ec1fea6bf9b3de5d146d298803d0412645d0248d" "q-106595/selection/b99a41c2495bc5629f5e19e5dd0eb7719a9a673afa058fcedfb87312b0b99f96"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-106595" :question/id #uuid "d0ce5fb8-1459-52f2-9308-99fa35085b85" :question/math-academy-id "q-106595" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14077122/assets/f8d67ac4521b6b7fbe5027e1fef52ab5d44763e558aef13e970dbc72aa2636d9.png)\n\nThe quarter-hyperbola above is defined by the parametric equations\n\n$$\nx=3\\operatorname{sec}⁡t,\\,y=\\sqrt{3}\\operatorname{tan}⁡t.\n$$\n\nWhat is the domain of the parameter $t?$" :question/worked-solution "The parametric equations of the full hyperbola are\n\n$$\nx=3\\operatorname{sec}⁡t,\\,y=\\sqrt{3}\\operatorname{tan}⁡t,\\,t\\in [-\\pi ,\\pi ],\\,t\\ne \\pm \\frac{\\pi }{2}.\n$$\n\nTo restrict the parameterization to a quarter-hyperbola, we refer to the diagram below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14077122/assets/b696475163cf9627709e62d8315edca393afd46aa2dbff5f23b4583e20641864.png)\n\nWe can see that if we restrict $t$ to $(-\\frac{\\pi }{2},0],$ we get the quarter-hyperbola.\n\nTherefore, the parametric equations that describe the required quarter-hyperbola are\n\n$$\nx=3\\operatorname{sec}⁡t,\\,y=\\sqrt{3}\\operatorname{tan}⁡t,\\,t\\in (-\\frac{\\pi }{2},0].\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-106595/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "14527450-9b34-5982-9d87-b5a31870a70e"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-106595"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "q-89345"] :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14077122/assets/90b505954bb714ad86f60e07f7a26c16c954139689d96684ed553a7b494f0527.png)\n\nOne branch of a hyperbola (shown above) is defined by the parametric equations\n\n$$\nx=\\sqrt{2}\\operatorname{sec}⁡t,\\,y=2\\operatorname{tan}⁡t.\n$$\n\nWhat is the domain of the parameter $t?$" :question/worked-solution "The parametric equations of the full hyperbola are\n\n$$\nx=\\sqrt{2}\\operatorname{sec}⁡t,\\,y=2\\operatorname{tan}⁡t,\\,t\\in [-\\pi ,\\pi ],\\,t\\ne \\pm \\frac{\\pi }{2}.\n$$\n\nTo restrict the parameterization to a single branch, we refer to the diagram below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14077122/assets/b43dcf6c343994e3226e2840a0ae80f60484c8de5d7984f61ec6447185181a76.png)\n\nWe can see that if we restrict $t$ to $(-\\frac{\\pi }{2},0]$ and $[0,\\frac{\\pi }{2}),$ we get only the right branch.\n\nTherefore, the parametric equations that describe only the right branch are\n\n$$\nx=4\\operatorname{sec}⁡t,\\,y=7\\operatorname{tan}⁡t,\\,t\\in (-\\frac{\\pi }{2},\\frac{\\pi }{2}).\n$$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "e-5378"] :question/problem "Given that the asymptotes of the hyperbola below are $y=\\pm\\dfrac{5}{7}x,$ find the parametric equations of the hyperbola.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14077122/assets/fd2618e961c15a9b0665e73e18544ab08b0d611b962bc3771558c61450cf49e5.png)" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "e-7896"] :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14077122/assets/6e12d114aedfd6c5c8ab5830e052fcc1dd3c937b825665a0490b42ca0c87972c.png)\n\nThe quarter-hyperbola above is defined by the parametric equations\n\n$$\nx = \\sqrt2\\sec{t}, \\qquad y = \\sqrt3\\tan{t}.\n$$\n\nWhat is the domain of the parameter $t?$" :question/worked-solution "The parametric equations of the full hyperbola are\n\n$$\nx= \\sqrt2 \\sec{t}, \\quad\ny = \\sqrt3 \\tan{t}, \\quad\nt \\in [-\\pi,\\pi], \\quad\nt \\neq \\pm\\dfrac{\\pi}2.\n$$\n\nTo restrict the parameterization to a quarter-hyperbola, we refer to the diagram below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14077122/assets/730325137cfca58eb17d65103e539d084f81d7ab810628261125c29dbb8a0284.png)\n\nWe can see that if we restrict $t$ to $\\left[0, \\dfrac{\\pi}2\\right)$ we get the required quarter-hyperbola.\n\nTherefore, the parametric equations that describe the required quarter-hyperbola are\n\n$$\nx= \\sqrt2\\sec{t}, \\quad\ny = \\sqrt3\\tan{t}, \\quad\nt \\in \\left[0, \\dfrac{\\pi}2\\right).\n$$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]}]
